1
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:05,340
Mum was coming round. I wanted to finish something for her.

2
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:07,765
A page for the family album.

3
00:00:13,267 --> 00:00:16,102
That's her, when she was five. The garden's still there.

4
00:00:16,317 --> 00:00:17,967
Her face is gone.

5
00:00:25,225 --> 00:00:27,550
Can you fill in the bit that's missing?

6
00:00:32,292 --> 00:00:34,457
And there she was. A little smile.

7
00:00:34,692 --> 00:00:37,382
I thought, yes. That looks like Mum.

8
00:00:43,750 --> 00:00:45,725
Could you try another one?

9
00:00:51,967 --> 00:00:53,967
This time, she wasn't smiling.

10
00:00:54,067 --> 00:00:55,792
I liked the first one better.

11
00:00:55,842 --> 00:00:57,892
But that didn't make it right.

12
00:01:05,983 --> 00:01:08,358
I asked why it had chosen a smile.

13
00:01:08,408 --> 00:01:10,358
The answer sounded reasonable.

14
00:01:10,408 --> 00:01:12,783
But it was still explaining a guess.

15
00:01:20,150 --> 00:01:23,825
If I put this in the album, someone might think it was real.

16
00:01:23,925 --> 00:01:26,550
In a few years, I might think so too.

17
00:01:32,667 --> 00:01:34,417
Then Mum arrived.

18
00:01:40,925 --> 00:01:42,575
Do you remember this?

19
00:01:44,525 --> 00:01:46,925
Oh, I don't remember that day.

20
00:01:50,025 --> 00:01:51,475
That's all right.

21
00:01:57,342 --> 00:01:59,292
I kept the old photograph.

22
00:01:59,342 --> 00:02:01,892
Beside the new one, I wrote: imagined.

23
00:02:01,967 --> 00:02:04,192
I didn't want to lose what was real.

24
00:02:09,708 --> 00:02:12,258
Mum was still sitting across from me.

25
00:02:15,508 --> 00:02:17,358
What was the garden like?

26
00:02:19,408 --> 00:02:21,558
There were roses by the back door.

27
00:02:21,718 --> 00:02:24,118
Your grandad was very proud of them.
